  "query_preview": "(Thursday through Sunday)...\nThe cooling trend will continue through Sunday with high\ntemperatures for inland areas next Sunday mostly 10 to 15 degrees\nbelow average. High temperatures for next Sunday will be mostly \nin the 60s to around 70 for the coast and valleys and for the \nmountains in the mid 30s to mid 50s.\n\nThe center of a closed low pressure center will be near the\nPacific Northwest coast for Thursday through Sunday. A nearly\nzonal subtropical jet stream from the central and eastern Pacific\ninto northern Baja will strengthen for Friday and Saturday,\npossibly transporting a low pressure into northern Baja into far \nsouthern California some time around late Saturday into Sunday. \nECMWF ensemble output increases precipitable water values in far \nsouthern California to 1.2 to 1.4 inches on Saturday afternoon and\nevening, around 200 to 250 percent of normal.\n\nFor Thursday through Sunday, the chance for measurable rainfall \nwill increase each day with chances for greater amounts increasing\nduring next weekend. For Saturday morning through Sunday night,\nThe chance of 1 inch or more of rainfall for the coast to the\nmountains is greater than 40 percent, and for San Diego County \nand the Riverside County mountains 50 to 60 percent. Chances for \n2 inches or more is mostly 25 to 35 percent for the coast to the \nmountains with chances for 3 inches or more 15 to 25 percent.",
